              "type_schema": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "submit_ruling",
        "doc": " LF-008: an appointed arbitrator rules on a DISPUTED line inside its own\n window only — primary in `[T0+N, T0+N+A)`, backup in\n `[T0+N+A, T0+N+A+B)` — with `buyer_amount + supplier_amount ==\n principal` (strict decimals, checked). Single writer: ALLOCATED and\n immutable. Allocation only between the original buyer and supplier;\n no token call (payouts are LF-009); E unchanged.",
        "kind": "call",
        "params": {
          "serialization_type": "json",
          "args": [
            {
              "name": "agreement_id",
              "type_schema": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            {
              "name": "line_id",
              "type_schema": {
                "type": "integer",
                "format": "uint32",
                "minimum": 0.0
              }
            },
            {
              "name": "buyer_amount",
              "type_schema": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            {
              "name": "supplier_amount",
              "type_schema": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "trigger_fallback",
        "doc": " LF-008: **any caller**, from `T0 + N + A + B`, applies the pre-agreed\n fallback split of the hashed terms (supplier = floor(P·bps/10 000),\n buyer = remainder). No amount parameters; result depends only on\n stored terms and chain time. Single writer; E unchanged.",
        "kind": "call",
        "params": {
          "serialization_type": "json",
          "args": [
            {
              "name": "agreement_id",
              "type_schema": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            {
              "name": "line_id",
              "type_schema": {
                "type": "integer",
                "format": "uint32",
                "minimum": 0.0
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "withdraw",
        "doc": " LF-009: the beneficiary withdraws their **whole** claimable amount on\n one ALLOCATED line. Caller must be the immutable `buyer_id` (for\n `BUYER`) or `supplier_id` (for `SUPPLIER`); the recipient is always that\n account. Requires exactly 1 yoctoNEAR (forwarded to `ft_transfer`) and\n enough prepaid gas for the transfer and the callback; both are checked\n before any state change. claimable → pending (E unchanged), then\n `ft_transfer` on the allowlisted token and the private callback, which\n alone decides PAID / FAILED. At most one open withdrawal per slot.",
        "kind": "call",
        "modifiers": [
          "payable"
        ],
        "params": {
          "serialization_type": "json",
          "args": [
            {
              "name": "agreement_id",
              "type_schema": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            {
              "name": "line_id",
              "type_schema": {
                "type": "integer",
                "format": "uint32",
                "minimum": 0.0
              }
            },
            {
              "name": "beneficiary",
              "type_schema": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "result": {
          "serialization_type": "json",
          "type_schema": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/Promise"
          }
        }
      }
